Because age is converged over time.
因为年龄随着时间的推移而趋同。

00:07:13.514 --> 00:07:14.495
That's what happens.
就是这样。

00:07:14.495 --> 00:07:16.846
So now you're both going in the other direction.
所以现在你们都朝着另一个方向前进。

00:07:16.846 --> 00:07:17.826
That's just science.
这就是科学。

00:07:17.826 --> 00:07:19.639
Craig is now five years older than I.
克雷格现在比我大五岁。

00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:23.920
All right, so I'm going to frame this for us here.
好吧，所以我要在这里为我们框架一下。

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:27.540
Eric's book, How the Arts Can Save Education is about many things.
埃里克的书《艺术如何拯救教育》讲述了很多事情。

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:33.959
But one is that classroom teaching techniques don't need to be siloed away from the rest of the world.
但其中之一是课堂教学技术不需要与世界其他地方隔绝。

00:07:33.959 --> 00:07:41.360
That teachers can use methods of sharing knowledge and skills in ways that other people do as well.
教师可以像其他人一样使用分享知识和技能的方法。

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:48.399
And specifically, she points to the arts and the way artists collaborate through improvisation, through trial and error, and through play.
具体而言，她指出了艺术以及艺术家通过即兴创作、反复试验和玩耍进行合作的方式。

00:07:48.399 --> 00:07:52.560
This is a great way to teach not just art, but math and science and everything else.
这不仅是教授艺术的好方法，也是教授数学、科学和其他一切的好方法。

00:07:52.560 --> 00:08:02.040
So the way we're looking at this, I'm looking at this, is that obviously making a television show is a highly collaborative, a constantly collaborative art form.
所以我们看待这个问题的方式，我看待这个问题的方式是，制作电视节目显然是一种高度协作、持续协作的艺术形式。

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:11.199
